  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for NRS_484B_587_1: all 7 witnesses pass, using 2 of the 6 gate runs.\n\n**The rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_587_1.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** the subject must be a vehicle under `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **When it applies:** some regulatory sign coded `entrance` or `exit` is in the scene, and the subject either starts or stops overlapping a controlled-access region at this observation.\n- **What it requires:** this holds for every controlled-access region.\n  - **Driving onto it:** the subject must be in a lane or other travel region that an entrance-coded sign governs.\n  - **Driving off it:** at the previous observation, the subject must have been inside the highway and in a region that an exit-coded sign governs. This is written exactly as the record states it.\n- I made no readings of my own, so no narrowings are declared.\n\n**The witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_587_1.lean`):\n- They share one map: the controlled-access area contains a mainline lane, an entrance ramp lane (entrance sign) and an exit ramp lane (exit sign), and there is a frontage road outside it.\n- Each trace has three observations 1 s apart. Every witness is judged only on the last two, because entering and leaving are detected by comparing with the previous observation.\n\n**Gate runs:**\n1. **VACUOUS**: no witness tested the \"entrance or exit\" sign-code check. `branch_3` had no signs at all, so the code was never read. I added a `keep_right` sign on the mainline. That still fits its narrative (\"no entrance- or exit-coded sign\") and makes the code check matter.\n2. **OK.**\n\n**One point for review:** the rule only requires an entrance or exit sign to be somewhere in the scene, as the record states. Nothing ties that sign to the subject. I expected the gate's unanchored-variable check might reject this, but it passed.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
